Hello. I have a set of microsatellite data for an hexaploid. I wanted to use adegenet and found that poppr had a very easy way to input data. I uploaded my data using poppr method and as a data frame though when i uploaded my data I found and extra allele in all loci. I have read that poppr can fix it using the command recode.polyploids. I want to do DAPC using my data but I believe this analysis is related to allele frequencies, should I use recode.polyploids before continuing or letting them as they are? adegenet tutorial doesn't take this into consideration.

